    description: "Bakeoff session organization (init -> cohort -> cycle -> iter-NNN) is currently 'tested in prod' rather than via integration tests. Build a test harness with mocked _run_cohort_repos that exercises: (a) init creates a fresh session, (b) cycle increments state.json iteration counter, (c) cycle creates iter-NNN/ subdirs in same session, (d) auto-discovery picks the latest session, (e) running cycle without prior cohort errors out cleanly. Mocking _run_cohort_repos lets us test the orchestration without actually running hypergumbo on repos. Per user note 2026-04-06: 'we haven't really put effort into doing integration tests of the bakeoff process itself and how runs and iterations progress and get recorded'. User explicitly approved deferring this as a tracker item."  # a657
